Z||000000||Fformula88||10-27-2000||11:30 PM||||I just got my next issue of Motor Trend and they drive a Speedster.  Unlike C&D last month, MT seems to think there is hope for the Speedster being imported for sale under Pontiac.  They also mention Saturn's desire, but the styling is already more in line with Pontiac.  Saturn wanted curvier styling.  <P>The best part is at the end.  The writer of the article (Jeff Bartlett) also pays a BIG compliment to the Fiero in the article.  Although there is no direct comparison of the two at all in his writeup... his last paragraph reads...<P>"If given the green light, we'd like to see the Fiero monicker brought back to life for the Speedster, with a turbocharged variant to wear the a GT badge."  (Motor Trend Magazine, Dec. 2000.  Pg. 94)<P>I have a feeling this will never happen.  Pontiac will do focus group studies and find the general public relates Fiero with fires... but it is nice to see a magazinewho wants to see the Fiero return.  (unlike Automobile and their awful editorial a couple months back).  <P>It also says they are doing a readers poll on  <A HREF="http://www.motortrend.com" TARGET=_blank>www.motortrend.com</A>   on whether they should sell the car in the US.  So everyone go and vote!  *** I went to the site and cannot find this poll, but I am leaving the link anyway in case someone else can find it.  It says it will ve there at the end of the article ***<P><BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">   <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<p>[This message has been edited by Fformula88 (edited 10-27-2000).]||||reg||1
